  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Namaa</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Agricultural land reclaimed from waterlogging and soil salinityIncreased water availability for irrigation from desalinated drainage waterSlope erosion and flash flood risk reduced through nature-based solutions600 farmers adopting water-smart practices and technologiesRegulatory SOP enabling legal reuse of drainage waterStrengthened institutional capacity of JVA and 8 Water User Associations180,000 people benefitting from improved water governance</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Namaa Project main goal is Improving subsurface water drainage, landscaping and water-smart agriculture in Northern Jordan Valley through integrated water resources management and innovative infrastructure, including 47 km of underground subsurface drainage. Key activities include restoring 900+ ha of degraded landscapes, promoting water-smart agriculture to 600 farmers, enhancing irrigation efficiency, and strengthening institutions and regulatory frameworks.These efforts aim to reduce water scarcity, soil degradation, and flood risks while improving biodiversity and climate resilience. By building institutional capacity and introducing new technologies, Namaa enhances food security, farmer incomes, and rural stability, benefiting over 180,000 people in the JV.The project is based on a direct request from the Jordan Valley Authority to support their mandate in water resource management and subsurface drainage.</narrative>
  </description>
